22\", \"text\": \"Assume L1: d_real>0. To prove the lower bound, assume for contradiction L2: k_real<d_real+1. Then 0≤k_real-1<d_real by F001. Put s_mid=(k_real-1+d_real)/2. These inequalities imply 0<s_mid<d_real and k_real<s_mid+1. The strict positivity of s_mid follows from d_real>0 even if k_real-1=0.\"}, {\"id\": \"S023\", \"text\": \"By F002, M002 applied to E at the nonnegative exponent s_mid gives H^s_mid(E)=∞, because dimH(E)=D is the cast of d_real. N003, applied with X=Rn(n₀), A=E and s=s_mid, gives H^s_mid(E)≤H^(s_mid+1)(F). Consequently H^(s_mid+1)(F)=∞.\"}, {\"id\": \"S024\", \"text\": \"M005 with A=F and the nonnegative exponent s_mid+1 yields s_mid+1≤T from F003, equivalently s_mid+1≤k_real by F001. This contradicts F002. Discharge L2 and conclude k_real≥d_real+1 under L1. Discharge L1, and combine with the d_real=0 implication in F001 by exhaustive cases on d_real≥0. Hence k_real≥d_real+1 for all cases.\"}, {\"id\": \"S025\", \"text\": \"F004 gives T≥D+1, and N005 gives T≤D+1. Antisymmetry proves T=D+1. Both dimensions and their sum are finite by F001 and N004. When n₀=0, N004 forces D=0 and the fibre branch already supplies the lower bound; the upper proof also covered this case. This proves the output proposition. Compactness remains an original hypothesis in the global specification, although this replacement proof does not use it.\"}], \"boundary\": \"Only listed inputs are project premises. The pinned Mathlib environment is freely available; no sibling proof is supplied.\", \"accepted_background_notes\": {\"R006.BG001\": {\"id\": \"BG001\", \"kind\": \"mathematical\", \"at\": \"/inference/argument/2/text\", \"fact\": \"A metric space, viewed as an emetric space by casting its distance, can be equipped with its Borel measurable structure without any condition on a specified subset. In particular this applies to Rn(n₀) and to MaxProd(Rn(n₀)); their subsets E and F need not be measurable to evaluate the supplied Hausdorff measures on them.\", \"grounds\": [{\"location\": \"/definitions/0/definition\", \"reason\": \"Rn(n₀) is the specified Euclidean metric space, including n₀=0.\"}, {\"location\": \"/definitions/8/definition\", \"reason\": \"MaxProd has the specified maximum product metric.\"}, {\"location\": \"/definitions/5/definition\", \"reason\": \"H is evaluated using the ambient Borel structure on arbitrary subsets.\"}], \"justification\": \"Every metric defines a topology and hence the sigma-algebra generated by its open sets; choosing that sigma-algebra is precisely choosing its Borel measurable structure. The maximum of the two coordinate distances is a metric: separation and symmetry hold coordinatewise, and max(a+c,b+d)≤max(a,b)+max(c,d) proves its triangle inequality from the coordinate triangle inequalities. Casting a finite metric distance gives the compatible emetric structure. These are ambient structure choices; no subset measurability or original hypothesis is added.\"}, \"R006.BG002\": {\"id\": \"BG002\", \"kind\": \"elementary\", \"at\": \"/inference/argument/2/text\", \"fact\": \"For u,v∈ℝ≥0∞, if u=∞ and u≤v then v=∞.\", \"grounds\": [{\"location\": \"/inputs/0/statement\", \"reason\": \"N003 compares H^s(E) to H^(s+1)(E×I) in ℝ≥0∞ for every positive s.\"}, {\"location\": \"/inputs/3/statement\", \"reason\": \"M002 gives infinite H^s(E) when the nonnegative exponent is below dimH(E).\"}, {\"location\": \"/inference/argument/0/produces/0/statement\", \"reason\": \"F001 identifies dimH(E) with the cast of d_real.\"}, {\"location\": \"/inference/argument/1/produces/0/statement\", \"reason\": \"F002 establishes 0<s_mid<d_real, enabling both cited inputs.\"}], \"justification\": \"Substitution gives ∞≤v. Since ∞ is the top element, also v≤∞; antisymmetry gives v=∞.\"}}, \"background_supplement_sha256\": \"b0996a24c8877cb2b28b0f59b0a5816651076241531dd94d6294843d68491feb\", \"objects\": [], \"representations\": [], \"bridges\": [], \"shared_inputs\": []}, \"has_more\": false, \"next_offset\": null}"}}
{"i":2,"result":{"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"id\": \"own-attempts.json\", \"pointer\": \"\", \"view\": \"value\", \"value\": [{\"kind\": \"proof\", \"candidate\": 1, \"sha256\": \"898debf70c30dd8e1cfe5c8148a1d9429bb75f4d3f406bb95611eee5a710ad8a\", \"actual_attempt\": {\"proof\": \"have hmeasure := @yui_aux_0001 n E h_T005 h_T006 h_T007\\nhave hconv := @yui_aux_0002 n E h_T005 h_T006 h_T007\\nobtain ⟨d, k, hd, hk, hk1⟩ := h_T006.2.2.2.2.2.2.2.2\\nhave hkreal : (1 : ℝ) ≤ (k : ℝ) := by exact_mod_cast hk1\\nhave hlowerReal : (d : ℝ) + 1 ≤ (k : ℝ) := by\\n  by_cases hz : (d : ℝ) = 0\\n  · linarith\\n  · have hdpos : 0 < (d : ℝ) := lt_of_le_of_ne d.property (Ne.symm hz)\\n    by_contra! hlt\\n    let s : ℝ := ((k : ℝ) - 1 + (d : ℝ)) / 2\\n    have hspos : 0 < s := by dsimp [s]; linarith\\n    have hsd : s < (d : ℝ) := by dsimp [s]; linarith\\n    have hks : (k : ℝ) < s + 1 := by dsimp [s]; linarith\\n    let a : ℝ≥0 := ⟨s, hspos.le⟩\\n    have ha : (a : ℝ≥0∞) < dimH E := by\\n      rw [← hd]\\n      exact (hconv a d).2.1.mpr hsd\\n    have hE : H s E = ⊤ := (hmeasure (BasisObjects.Rn n) E a).1 ha\\n    have htrans : H s E ≤ H (s + 1) (F n E) :=\\n      (h_T005 (BasisObjects.Rn n) E s hspos).2\\n    have hF : H (s + 1) (F n E) = ⊤ := top_unique (hE ▸ htrans)\\n    let b : ℝ≥0 := ⟨s + 1, by linarith⟩\\n    have hb : (b : ℝ≥0∞) ≤ dimH (F n E) :=\\n      (hmeasure (BasisObjects.Rn n × ℝ) (F n E) b).2 hF\\n    rw [← hk] at hb\\n    have hbReal : s + 1 ≤ (k : ℝ) := (hconv b k).1.mp hb\\n    linarith\\nhave hlower : dimH E + 1 ≤ dimH (F n E) := by\\n  rw [← hd, ← hk, ← (hconv d k).2.2]\\n  apply (hconv (d + 1) k).1.mpr\\n  simpa only [NNReal.coe_add, NNReal.coe_one] using hlowerReal\\nhave heq : dimH (F n E) = dimH E + 1 := le_antisymm h_T007.1 hlower\\nrefine ⟨heq, h_T007.2.1, h_T007.2.2, ?_⟩\\nrw [← heq]\\nexact h_T007.2.2\", \"statement\": \"dimH (F n E) = dimH E + 1 ∧ dimH E < ⊤ ∧\\n  dimH (F n E) < ⊤ ∧ dimH E + 1 < ⊤\", \"proof_package\": {\"schema\": \"yui-local-proof